{
  "$comment": "Per-route Firestore read ceilings for src/app/api/**/route.ts. Enforced by scripts/check-read-ceilings.mjs (npm run check:read-ceilings). One line per route: to lower a ceiling, edit only that route's line and lower config/read-ceilings.baseline.json in the same commit.",
  "version": 1,
  "countedAtBase": "12cf0689 + structural integration stack (final merged tree, 2026-10-30)",
  "unit": "statically-counted Firestore read call-sites in the route's OWN file (see countedShapes); NOT runtime read volume - one call-site inside a loop or chunking helper costs many runtime reads (e.g. src/app/api/users/picker/route.ts: 2 call-sites, ~450-500 runtime reads per cold build).",
  "countedShapes": [
    "adminGet: .get() with no arguments (Query/DocumentReference .get(), incl. .count().get() aggregations)",
    "txGet: t.get(ref) / tx.get(ref) / trx.get(ref) / transaction.get(ref)",
    "getAll: .getAll(...)",
    "clientSdk: getDoc( / getDocs( / getCountFromServer( / onSnapshot( in a server route file",
    "comments are stripped before counting; a comment mentioning a read shape is not a call-site"
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "ROUTE FILE ONLY: reads performed inside lib helpers (src/lib/**) that a route calls are NOT counted. Example at this base: src/app/api/admin/audit-logs/route.ts scores 0 because its Firestore reads run inside createFirestoreAuditAdapter (src/lib/server/admin-audit-firestore.ts), not in the route file.",
    "Seam-only routes score 0: a route whose own file only calls the Supabase seam (or a lib helper) is a 0 entry even when the seam's Firestore fallback path reads behind the flag.",
    "Call-sites, not volume: the gate bounds the SHAPE of the code (how many distinct read sites a route may grow), which is the part a code change controls. Runtime volume per call-site is the quota-guard canary's and the census's job, not this gate's."
  ],
  "census": "The census allowlist is exactly the set of routes below with firestoreReads > 0. It is shrink-only against config/read-ceilings.baseline.json.",
